  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (scvi_n200, multi-profile, avgpool) is the current best at 0.650 acc, and we know avgpool > transformer for PCA (config_002 vs 003). However, it is untested whether this aggregation preference holds for scvi_n200, whose learned latent representations may interact differently with transformer attention vs. simple averaging. Question: Does transformer aggregation improve or degrade performance when paired with the strongest RNA encoder (scvi_n200)? This is a single-variable change from the current best (config_005 → config_006), cleanly isolating the aggregation effect. Why best next: It reduces uncertainty about a design choice that directly informs every future multimodal experiment (configs 032/033 use scvi_n200 + transformer, configs 030/031 use avgpool). Resolving this before committing budget to multimodal fusion ensures we build on the correct RNA-side foundation, and it is lower-risk than jumping to a multimodal config where the weak image signal (ResNet50 at 0.208) could confound the interpretation."
}

